    advanced: 'Theoretical Card Counting: In theory, if playing with a single deck and cards are not reshuffled between rounds, one could track which ranks have been depleted. However, with multiple decks (the standard), this is practically impossible.',
    tips: [
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "If you are the Banker, your edge is entirely in the initial deal. If you don't hit a matching pair in the first two cards, your odds drop to approximately 50-50.",
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: 'The faster the game is played, the more dangerous it is for your bankroll. Take your time between rounds.',
      },
      {
        title: 'Tip',
        description: "Never chase losses in a pure chance gameâ€”the odds don't 'owe' you anything.",
